# ThreadSanitizer suppressions, used by `zig build test -Dtsan=true`.
#
# processWebsocketData releases `processing` and then re-arms the socket with
# epoll_ctl(EPOLL_CTL_MOD, ..., EPOLLONESHOT). Another worker can only receive
# the connection after that re-arm, so the kernel orders the two threads. TSan
# only treats EPOLL_CTL_ADD as a release (not MOD), so it can't see this and
# reports races between rearmRead and whatever the next worker does with the
# connection (acquireProcessing, close, freeing the HandlerConn).
race:rearmRead
